    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d4">

                <pb facs="0132" n="4" sameAs="frus:frus1885/pg4"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">No. 4.</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Mr.
                            Osborn</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1885-05-25"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 25,
                        1885</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 227.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I inclose a copy of the material portion of
                    a letter from Mr. Scrymser, president of the Central and South American
                    Telegraph Company, 37 Wall street, New York, in continuation of the subject of
                    the proposed extension of the telegraphic lines now existing to Brazil,
                    presented in a recent telegram to you.</p>
                <p>Please investigate the entire matter of the scheme and report. You can properly
                    make known to the Argentine Government the general desire in this country and
                    the wish of the Government for full and unimpeded telegraphic communication
                    between the United States and the Argentine Republic.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>T. F. BAYARD.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d4-a1.xml" xpointer="d4-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
